From 50d027bc7c23bd84da951f9fac7b2d920db9ffa7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jakompiled <itsrufer@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 16:15:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/10] goalc: wasm object files and a uniform GOAL function
 type

goalc-wasm can now write a GOAL v3 object for the wasm runtime: static
data, an 8-byte function object per function (table index, and for the
top-level function the offset of the embedded module) and the wasm
module at the end of the top-level segment. Static and function
addresses are segment base imports plus offsets; each module exports
__link, which adds its functions to the table.

Every GOAL function now has the wasm type (i64 x 8) -> i64 and callers
pad with zeros, because GOAL code calls functions with more or fewer
arguments than they take, which x86 tolerates and call_indirect doesn't.
---
